.* ------------------------------------------------------------ examples
:HELP NAME='WRKXDBPRF/COMMAND/EXAMPLES'.
Examples for WRKXDBPRF - Help
:XH3.Examples for WRKXDBPRF
:P.
:HP2.Example 1&colon. Showing the profiles:EHP2.
:XMP.
WRKXDBPRF
:EXMP.
:P.
This command shows the list of the connection profiles.
:P.
:HP2.Example 2&colon. Making a PostgreSQL database available:EHP2.
:OL.
:LI.
Run WRKXDBPRF and press F6. Type RDB name SALESPG, database type
PG, the host, the database and the user, and press Enter.
:LI.
Press F10 and type the password twice.
:LI.
Back on the list, type 9 next to SALESPG. The window shows the
version of the server.
:LI.
Type 8 next to SALESPG to add the RDB directory entry.
:LI.
In interactive SQL, or in a program created with RDB(SALESPG), run
CONNECT TO SALESPG.
:EOL.
:P.
:HP2.Example 3&colon. Installing XDBARDDRV from a package:EHP2.
:XMP.
CRTLIB LIB(XDB)
RSTOBJ OBJ(*ALL) SAVLIB(CESCO2) DEV(*SAVF) SAVF(QGPL/XDBSAVF)
       RSTLIB(XDB)
ADDLIBLE LIB(XDB)
WRKXDBPRF
:EXMP.
:P.
The Setup display is shown because the profile files are not there
yet. F10 goes through what is to do; every step shows its commands
and waits for Enter.
:P.
:HP2.Example 4&colon. Closing a database for a while:EHP2.
:P.
Type 2 next to the profile and set Status to D. Every CONNECT TO is
refused until the status is A again. Connections that are open go
on.
:EHELP.
.* -------------------------------------------------------------- errors
:HELP NAME='WRKXDBPRF/ERROR/MESSAGES'.
Error messages for WRKXDBPRF - Help
:XH3.Error messages for WRKXDBPRF
:P.
:HP3.*ESCAPE Messages:EHP3.
:P.
None. What the command has to say is shown on the message line of
its displays.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
